course: dictionary
lesson: 15453
title: Stillness and calm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stillness is a noun, a word for a state. It means being completely still, with no movement, or being quiet and calm, with no noise. Look at the words around it for clues. «In the stillness, Maya could hear her own heartbeat.» Maya could hear her heartbeat because everything else was quiet and still, so stillness means calm and silent.
explain: Writers use stillness to set a scene. «The stillness of the frozen lake was broken only by a single crack.» The lake is not moving, and the crack is a surprise. Test your meaning by swapping in «calm» or «no movement» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Stillness also helps people feel calm. In mindfulness lessons, children practise stillness by sitting quietly and noticing their breath. Stillness is about being still and calm, with no noise, so it is different from a dull or boring moment.
fact: Stillness is a noun, so it names a state or quality.
fact: «Stillness» means being completely still, with no movement.
fact: «Stillness» also means being quiet and calm, with no noise.
fact: The word is built from «still» and the ending «-ness», which turns an adjective into a noun.
fact: Common phrases are «the stillness of the night» and «in the stillness».
exercise: «The stillness of the frozen lake was broken only by a single crack.» What does stillness mean here? | A cold, wet wind | *No movement, completely still | Loud splashing and big waves | Bright sunshine on the water
exercise: «In the stillness of the library, Sam could hear the clock tick.» Why can Sam hear the clock? | Because the clock was very loud and broken | Because Sam was running around the room | Because the library was full of shouting people | *Because the room was so quiet that a tiny tick could be heard
exercise: Which word could replace stillness in «the stillness of the night» without changing the meaning? | bustle | *calm | loudness | rush
test: «The pond had no ripples, and the stillness made it look like glass.» What does stillness mean? | Noisy ducks flying over | Lots of waves and splashing | *Completely still, with no movement | Dirty, muddy water
test: Which is the best way to practise stillness in a mindfulness lesson? | Shout your favourite song | Run around the playground as fast as you can | Jump up and down ten times | *Sit quietly for a minute with no moving or talking
exam: «After the storm, a deep stillness filled the forest, and not a leaf moved.» Which is the best meaning of stillness here? | *Complete calm, with no movement and no noise | Loud thunder rolling across the sky | A busy market full of people | Strong wind and heavy rain
